  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe blocker from the maintainer's review of #512 reached main when #512 merged at 7e39726.\n\n`recognize::pockets_of` read \"up\" and \"leans into\" straight off the facet winding. So an inside-out 10 mm cube came back as `Pocket { kind: Closed, floor_z: 0, depth: 10, boundary: the part's outline }`, and `detect_pockets create` would cut the whole footprint to the base.\n\n`pockets_of` now runs #387's body-winding verdict (`pick::winding::winding_of` / `verdict_for`) over the whole model first. Any body whose outside can't be trusted is refused by name, in recognition's own words: inside-out, open (torn), non-manifold, mixed winding, flat, or no readable facet.\n\n`docs/decisions/718-pocket-winding.md` records the choices: why whole-model and not per-pocket, and why the refusal has its own wording instead of `refusal()`'s \"before aligning to it\".\n\n## Pinned by\n\n- `pocket_recognition::an_inside_out_mesh_is_refused_never_read_as_a_pocket`. A reversed cube and a reversed pocket block are refused with \"inside-out\", and the same block wound outward still reads its one pocket. **It fails without the fix:** the reversed cube reads as a 10 mm closed pocket.\n- `pocket_recognition::degenerate_input_refuses_cleanly`: the torn half-pocket now expects the \"open body\" refusal. Before, it only checked for no panic.\n\n## How tested\n\nOn upstream main plus this commit:\n- `pocket_recognition` 11/11, `mcp_pockets` 3/3, `mcp` 13/13 and `pick` 9/9 pass;\n- the ui lib pocket tests pass;\n- clippy `-D warnings` is clean on the app lib and `pocket_recognition`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo GUI run. Recognition has no UI entry point yet (#511).\n\nThe fork is synced at v0.16.0; the branch is cut from upstream/main.\n\nChangelog: Pocket recognition refuses an inside-out or open mesh by name instead of reading its outline as a pocket (#718)\n\nFixes #718\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
